# The PrismPM revision `prismpm build` is made by in .github/workflows/lexlean.yml,
# the only place it is written (AGENTS.md R1), like .github/lexlean.rev. The
# workflow builds `prismpm` at this commit and builds the conformance server
# application with it (conformance/, prismpm.toml).
#
# The LexLean it is built with is not the one PrismPM vendors but the revision of
# .github/lexlean.rev, so one pin drives both tools: the vendored lexlean (cee0fbade)
# cannot read this repository's sources (LLP2001 on `term_cases`, src/Json.lex.tex:230),
# and `JsonWriteLaws` uses `nested_induction`, which only SM-37 and later has. Nothing
# in PrismPM changes; the workflow replaces vendor/lexlean in its own copy of the tree
# (.github/lexlean-ci/lib.sh, `install_prismpm`; CI.md).
#
# The pin moves to the PrismPM SDK release before MCP v0.1.0, and that release must
# pin a LexLean release that contains SM-37.
#
# Currently: UOR-Foundation/PrismPM#339 at its head, the `ServerApplication` model,
# the server build and the host packages.
rev = f5927bf46b92179d807ee6bf987f024b2f5a4e7e
